id: records/epistemic-status-drift-ledger-2026-08-28
title: "Epistemic-status vocabulary drift — cross-root scan and containment"
kind: observation-record
status: reported_pending_dave_acceptance
recorded_at: 2026-08-28
recorded_by: agent:anthropic:claude-code
epistemic_status: observed

observation: >
  A deterministic scan across the three roots on 2026-08-28 found the
  epistemic_status field drifted into 50+ ad-hoc values against the
  ontology's seven (observed | reported | inferred | assumed | predicted |
  disputed | unknown). Counts of non-canonical scalar values: this canon
  repository 6 (now grandfathered and test-locked), dave.yawn/Yawns ~54
  (dominant strains: proposed x14, reported_plus_inferred x13),
  web-game/YAWNS ~25 (observed_with_labeled_inference x9,
  observed_and_inferred x8). One apparent violation
  (epistemic_status: true in YAWN_COGNITIVE_CONTAINER_RUNTIME.yawn) is a
  false positive - a contract requirement flag, not a status value.

root_cause: >
  templates/full.yawn taught a divergent vocabulary (supported/unproven
  present, predicted absent), so authors composing nuance had no sanctioned
  place for it and minted composite statuses inline. Free-text statuses make
  records uncomputable by rankers, graduation ladders, and claim calculators.

containment: >
  This proposal fixes the template, adds
  tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs locking this repository to the
  seven values with an explicit shrink-only grandfather ledger, and records
  this drift map. It does NOT rewrite any existing record - history is
  preserved; migration of each grandfathered record belongs to its author.

proposed_convention: >
  epistemic_status holds exactly one of the seven values. Composite nuance
  moves to epistemic_note (free text) or per-claim attribution blocks.
  Downstream roots (dave.yawn, web-game/YAWNS) adopt the same checker after
  Dave accepts this convention; their legacy values migrate opportunistically
  when records are next touched, never in bulk.

boundary: >
  Proposal until the principal rules. No record content was rewritten; the
  only mutated file is the template's teaching comment.
